            "material": "1. W: Hey, Mike, what do you think of the museum you visited today?\n2. M: Hey, Sue. The museum is great, very interesting. They have loads of stuff there on display. The primitive tools early humans used tell a lot about their life, but my favorite is the coin collection. They have some coins that are over 2,000 years old.\n3. W: That sounds cool.\n4. M: Yeah, what did you do today?\n5. W: Kathy and I just wandered through the old city centre. The streets are narrow but beautiful with plenty of charm. We saw the Trevi Fountain, which is in all the guidebooks.\n6. M: How do you like it?\n7. W: It's very pretty, but it was overcrowded with tourists.\n8. M: Yeah, well, it's crowded everywhere. It is August after all, the busiest month of the year.\n9. W: Yes, it's like the whole world is here on holiday, including us. What will you do tomorrow?\n10. M: I haven't decided yet. I was thinking of doing what you did today—wandering the old streets and taking pictures. I was also thinking of visiting the square with the Spanish steps.\n11. W: What is that? I haven't heard of it.\n12. M: It's a square where on one side, there are some very wide steps with flowers that go up to a church. It's also in all the tourist guidebooks. It's very famous and pretty. I was also thinking of seeing that tomorrow.\n13. W: It sounds very nice. Do you mind if Kathy and I join you tomorrow?\n14. M: Not at all. I spent the whole day today pretty much alone. Doing tourist stuff with others would be a welcome change.\n15. W: Let me ask her first, but I'm sure she'll be up for it.",
