            "label": "Banked Cloze",
            "material": "It may sound surprising, but people who are supersensitive to coffee's bitter taste actually drink more of it, a new study finds. This sensitivity isn't ___26___ a matter of taste, either, but rather is influenced by a person's genetic makeup, the researchers said in the study. \"You'd expect that people who are particularly sensitive to the bitter taste of caffeine would drink less coffee,\" said study senior researcher Marilyn Cornelis. \"The ___27___ results of our study suggest coffee consumers acquire a taste for or an ability to detect the bitterness of caffeine due to the learned positive ___28___ brought out by caffeine.\" Put another way, people who have a ___29___ ability to taste the bitterness of coffee learn to associate \"good things with it,\" Cornelis said. This finding is surprising, given that bitterness often serves as a warning mechanism to ___30___ people to spit out harmful substances, the scientists said. Researchers conducted the study to understand how genetics influences people's ___31___ of tea, coffee and alcohol which tend to taste bitter, said lead researcher Jue Sheng Ong. \"While all bitter flavors may seem the same, we ___32___ the bitterness of Brussels sprouts(抱子甘蓝), quinine(奎宁) and caffeine ___33___ ,\" Ong told Live Science. \"The degree to which we find these flavors bitter is, in part, determined by your genes.\" People with the genes to taste the bitterness of green vegetables are more likely to prefer tea to coffee. In ___34___ , people who were more sensitive to quinine's bitter flavors and those found in green vegetables tended to ___35___ coffee.",
            "translationCn": "一项新的研究发现，这听起来可能令人惊讶，但那些对咖啡苦味极其敏感的人实际上喝的咖啡更多。\n研究人员在这项研究中表示，这种敏感性也不只是味觉问题，而是受到一个人基因构成的影响。\n“你可能会认为，那些对咖啡因苦味特别敏感的人会少喝咖啡。”该研究的资深研究员玛丽莲·科内利斯说，“我们的研究结果却恰恰相反，这表明，由于咖啡因带来的后天习得的积极强化作用，咖啡饮用者逐渐喜欢上了咖啡因的苦味，或者具备了辨别这种苦味的能力。”\n换句话说，科内利斯说，那些对咖啡苦味的感知能力更强的人会学着把“美好的事物与之联系起来”。科学家们表示，鉴于苦味通常会起到警示作用，使人们吐出有害物质，这一发现令人惊讶。\n首席研究员邬觉生说，研究人员开展这项研究，是为了了解基因如何影响人们对茶、咖啡和酒精的饮用量，因为这些饮品往往尝起来是苦的。\n邬觉生告诉《生命科学》：“尽管所有苦味似乎都一样，但我们会分别感知抱子甘蓝、奎宁和咖啡因的苦味。我们觉得这些味道有多苦，部分取决于你的基因。”\n拥有能够感知绿色蔬菜苦味的基因的人更有可能偏爱茶而不是咖啡。此外，那些对奎宁的苦味以及绿色蔬菜中的苦味更敏感的人往往会避免喝咖啡。",
