                "analysis": "【答案】 C （细节题） It brought the mine's operations to a halt. 【定位】 P7 A company spokesperson said the operations at the site had been halted while the investigation is ongoing and that the break had posed no safety threat to workers. 公司发言人表示，调查期间该矿区已停止作业，并称这次坝体破裂并未对工人构成任何安全威胁。 【信号】 spokesperson said 引述信号词 。第 7 段开头 A company spokesperson said 是最强的引述信号，直接告诉考生「下面这句就是发言人的原话」。句中包含两个并列宾语从句（halted while investigation + no safety threat），把「停产」和「对工人无安全威胁」一并说出，正是第 2 题的答案句。 【替换】 the operations at the site had been halted ↔ It brought the mine's operations to a halt. 被动 ↔ 主动 + 动词名词化 had to be temporarily suspended on Friday ↔ It brought the mine's operations to a halt. suspend = halt 【排除】 A) 与原文相反 录音第 7 段明确说 the break had posed no safety threat to workers——发言人特意强调「没有」构成安全威胁。选项 A 把 posed、safety threat 这几个高辨识度原词原样照搬，唯独把 no 去掉，含义彻底反转。这是听力里最经典的「否定词陷阱」。 借用原文：the break had posed no safety threat to workers B) 过度推断 录音第 6 段说 said it was conducting a thorough investigation——公司正在做全面调查；选项 B 却把「在调查」升级成「损失大到无法评估」 It caused damage too heavy to assess.，凭空加上了 too heavy to assess 这一程度判断，原文无任何依据。 借用原文：said it was conducting a thorough investigation D) 原词陷阱 录音第 2 段说 The wall collapse at the Cadia mine came just a few days after two earthquakes hit the area.——坝塌发生在两次地震「之后」（事件 ← 两次地震在前）；选项 D It was followed by two more earthquakes. 却说「这次事件之后又有两次地震」，时序刚好相反，更多了 more 这个原文没有的词。选项 D 把 two earthquakes 这个原词盗过来，把时序对调。 借用原文：The wall collapse at the Cadia mine came just a few days after two earthquakes hit the area."
