                "analysis": "【答案】 B （主旨题） How to make progress in one's career. 【定位】 P1 M: Welcome to \"Business Matters\". Today we have invited career development consultant Lucy Williams to talk about how to get ahead at work. Hi, Lucy. Many of us never seem to get promoted. Why is that? And what can we do about it? 男：欢迎来到《Business Matters》。今天我们邀请了职业发展顾问 Lucy Williams 来谈谈如何在职场上取得进步。嗨，Lucy。很多人似乎一直得不到晋升。为什么会这样？我们能做些什么？ 【信号】 开头点题句 。主持人开场即点明 “to talk about how to get ahead at work”，how to get ahead at work 直接给出对话主题；后续多次出现的 promoted、career 等词进一步锁定。 【替换】 how to get ahead at work ↔ How to make progress in one's career. 同义改写：get ahead = make progress；at work = in one's career 【排除】 A) 原词陷阱 How to run one's business successfully. 中的 business 来自节目名 “Business Matters”，但对话讲的是职场晋升，不是如何经营自己的企业；属于用原文出现的 business 原词设陷阱。 借用原文：Business Matters C) 过度推断 Why few people can fully display their capabilities. 中 “few people can fully display capabilities” 在录音中并未出现，属于用 “never seem to get promoted” 过度推断出的伪主题。 D) 原词陷阱 Why young people seldom get the expected promotion. 盗用了 Many of us never seem to get promoted. 中的 promoted，但全文讨论的是 “how to get ahead” 而不仅是 “why young people don't get promoted”，属于以偏概全。 借用原文：Many of us never seem to get promoted."
