            "material": "Two proposals are before the state legislature that look to put some limits on ever-increasing rent prices, which some lawmakers say are contributing to rising homelessness rates. The proposals ___26___ caps on rent increases, preventing landlords in the state from raising rent more than the rate of inflation in most cases. There are exceptions for buildings less than 10 years old, public housing, improvements beyond maintenance, and a hardship ___27___ . In a 2020 study, researchers at the U.S. Government Accountability Office estimated that every $100 in rent increase is ___28___ to a 9% rise in homelessness. Rent increases have an even more detrimental effect on some demographic groups, such as racial minorities. Representative Alex Ramel explained why he thought that this kind of legislation was so important, telling the story of a ___29___ struggling to live in the community. Ramel pointed out the ___30___ effect of double-digit rent increases, saying that he made the decision to introduce the legislation while talking to a young man in Bellingham. \"He's a recent graduate from Western Washington University and just got a new job,\" Ramel said. \"He was leaving our community because his landlord ___31___ him that his rent was going to go up by $600 a month.\" The Rental Housing Association of Washington opposes the legislation. The association ___32___ that the policy won't actually solve the problem of rental prices. Instead, it will punish small landlords and allow wealthy renters easy access to cheap housing. \"The rent control policy has failed everywhere it has been ___33___ in this county. It has not fixed one housing problem ___34___ . It also does not distinguish between rich and poor when ___35___ who gets the benefits of rent control,\" said Chester Baldwin with the Rental Housing Coalition.",
            "translationCn": "州议会目前正在审议两项提案，旨在对不断上涨的租金设置一些限制。一些议员表示，租金上涨正在导致无家可归率上升。\n这些提案对租金涨幅设定上限，在大多数情况下，禁止该州房东将租金涨幅提高到超过通货膨胀率的水平。例外情况包括建成未满10年的建筑、公共住房、维护之外的改造，以及因困难而获得的豁免。\n在2020年的一项研究中，美国政府问责署的研究人员估计，租金每上涨100美元，就与无家可归率上升9%相关。租金上涨对某些人口群体的影响更加不利，例如少数族裔。\n亚历克斯·拉梅尔议员讲述了一名努力在当地社区生活的选民的故事，并解释了他为何认为这类立法如此重要。\n拉梅尔指出，两位数租金涨幅会造成毁灭性影响。他说，自己是在与贝灵厄姆的一名年轻人交谈时决定提出这项立法的。拉梅尔说：“他刚从西华盛顿大学毕业，最近找到了一份新工作。他正要离开我们的社区，因为他的房东通知他，租金每月要上涨600美元。”\n华盛顿州租赁住房协会反对这项立法。该协会声称，这项政策实际上无法解决租金问题，反而会惩罚小房东，让富裕租户轻易获得廉价住房。\n租赁住房联盟的切斯特·鲍德温说：“租金管制政策在这个国家所有实施过的地方都失败了。它没有在任何地方解决一个住房问题。在决定谁能从租金管制中受益时，它也不区分富人和穷人。”",
