            "groupCn": "选词填空",
            "label": "Banked Cloze",
            "material": "Most financial crises have plenty in common: they tend to start in the banking sector and involve excessive borrowing, together with an asset bubble. The ___26___ crisis of 2008 was no different, with the asset bubble focused on US real estate. But my research suggests this crisis had another ___27___ cause—that some people in the banking sector were playing or \"gaming\" the system for their own financial gain. The game being played had several important features. The first was the deliberate complexity of the financial products at its core. Then there are the ___28___ biases that permeate decision-making at all levels of the banking industry. Banking often attracts people with certain personality ___29___ , including those who are overconfident and take excessive risks. Such people tend to like complexity for its own sake, but they often do not fully understand the ___30___ of that complexity for the stability of the financial system as a whole. Often they do not care—they are primarily interested in gaming the system to ___31___ their bonuses. The next element is risk. There are parts of the banking sector that will always be ___32___ to risk, but many bankers have come to feel immune to its potential impact, because they ___33___ that, however recklessly banks behave, governments will always be there to bail them out. Gaming in the banking sector seems virtually impossible to ___34___ . The only effective measure to end it would be to make bankers ___35___ liable for losses, but no government has ever passed such a law, and no single government could do so on its own, since this would immediately cause their entire national banking sector to move wholesale to another jurisdiction.",
            "translationCn": "大多数金融危机都有许多共同之处：它们往往始于银行业，并伴随着过度借贷和资产泡沫。2008年的全球危机也不例外，只是当时的资产泡沫集中在美国房地产市场。但我的研究表明，这场危机还有另一个根本原因——银行业中的一些人为了谋取个人经济利益而操纵或“钻”制度的空子。\n当时所进行的这种操纵具有几个重要特征。首先是其核心金融产品经过了刻意设计，十分复杂。其次，行为偏差渗透到了银行业各个层面的决策过程中。银行业往往会吸引具有某些性格特征的人，其中包括过度自信、过度承担风险的人。\n这类人往往会为了复杂而复杂地追求复杂性，但他们通常并不完全理解这种复杂性对整个金融体系稳定性的影响。很多时候，他们并不在乎这些影响——他们主要关心的是操纵制度，以使自己的奖金最大化。\n下一个要素是风险。银行业中有些领域始终容易受到风险影响，但许多银行家逐渐觉得自己不会受到风险潜在影响，因为他们认定，无论银行的行为多么鲁莽，政府总会出手救助它们。\n银行业中的这种制度操纵几乎不可能被消除。终结这种行为的唯一有效措施，是让银行家个人对损失承担责任；但从未有任何政府通过这样的法律，而且任何单一政府也无法独自这样做，因为这会立即导致本国整个银行业大规模迁往其他司法管辖区。",
