                "analysis": "【答案】 K 段（强锚点） 【锚点】 Breedcafs / coffee farms 【定位】 K 段 A global project called Breedcafs is studying how trees behave in coffee farms, hoping to find crop varieties that manage to grow under the shade of trees. Coffee grows naturally in such forests, so copying that in farms is taking the crop back to its roots. 'By reintroducing trees in the landscape, we impact positively humidity, rain capture, soil conservation and biodiversity preservation,' says coffee expert Benoit Bertrand, who leads the project from the French Agricultural Research Centre for International Development. Bertrand is analysing which of dozens of coffee varieties fits better for this system. 一個名為 Breedcafs 的全球項目正在研究咖啡農場中樹木的生長情況，希望找到能在樹蔭下生長的作物品種。咖啡天然生長於這樣的森林中，因此在農場中模仿這種做法等於讓作物回歸本源。「通過在景觀中重新引入樹木，我們積極影響濕度、雨水截留、土壤保護和生物多樣性保護，」在法國農業國際合作研究中心領導該項目的咖啡專家 Benoit Bertrand 說。Bertrand 正在分析數十種咖啡品種中哪一種更適合這一系統。 【改写】 A study is under way across the world ↔ A global project called Breedcafs is studying 同義改寫 to look for crops that can grow among trees ↔ hoping to find crop varieties that manage to grow under the shade of trees 同義替換＋語境細化 【辨邻】 J agroforestry (a system of land use in which harvestable trees or shrubs are grown among or around crops or on pasture land) 雖涉及 crops 與 trees，但沒有 Breedcafs、coffee farms 或研究品種的內容。 agroforestry (a system of land use in which harvestable trees or shrubs are grown among or around crops or on pasture land)"
