                "analysis": "【答案】 D （细节题） The medical community. 【定位】 P6 My last book was written primarily for the medical community. But this time, I want to help ordinary people take control of their weight. 我上一本书主要是为医学界写的。但这一次，我想帮助普通人掌控自己的体重。 【信号】 限定词 last + 受众句，并与 \"this time\" 对照 。答案信号是 My last book was written primarily for the medical community 这句明确的 \"上一本 written for 谁\"，紧接的 But this time 形成 \"上一本 vs 这一本\" 对照，提醒要选 last 对应的那一群。 【替换】 My last book was written primarily for the medical community ↔ The medical community 受众原词直接对应 【排除】 A) 张冠李戴 The general public. 对应的是 this time, I want to help ordinary people——那是 \"这一本(新书)\" 的受众。把 this time 的受众安到 last book 头上，正是没分清两本书的张冠李戴。 借用原文：this time, I want to help ordinary people take control of their weight B) 原词陷阱 Those who are overweight. 借了通篇出现的 overweight 一词，但录音从没说哪本书是 \"为超重者\" 而写；它只是话题词，不是 last book 的受众。 借用原文：more than 60% of Americans are overweight C) 答非所问 Those who want to lose weight. 贴合全场减肥主题、最顺耳，但录音说 last book 是写给 medical community 的；\"想减肥的人\" 从未被点名为某本书的受众，是借主题诱选。"
