                "analysis": "【答案】 B （态度观点题） She tries to force people to accept her radical ideas. 【定位】 P3 Critics of your book assert that you're trying to force radical changes on the entire country. Some claim that you want to force everyone to eat a vegetarian diet and make private transport illegal. 你这本书的批评者断言，你想把激进的改变强加给整个国家。有人声称你想强迫所有人吃素食、把私人交通工具变成非法。 【信号】 Critics assert 转述信号 。出现 Critics of your book assert that 这一转述信号，明确告诉你下面就是批评者的说法，正对题干的 critics，是答案句标志。 【替换】 you're trying to force radical changes on the entire country ↔ She tries to force people to accept her radical ideas. 几近同词的核心保留 【排除】 A) 未提及 She neglects people's efforts in animal protection. 提到 animal protection 蹭了动物话题，但批评者从没说她「忽视他人的动保努力」，原文无此评价。 C) 原词陷阱 She ignores the various benefits of public transport. 用了反复出现的 public transport，但批评者根本没说她「无视公共交通的好处」——恰恰相反，她是支持公共交通的，这是把话题词乱拼成的指控。 借用原文：make private transport illegal D) 张冠李戴 She insists vegetarians are harming the environment. 用了 vegetarian 和 environment 两个高频词，但批评者说的是她想强迫大家吃素，绝非说「素食者在破坏环境」，意思被拧反了。 借用原文：you want to force everyone to eat a vegetarian diet"
