                "analysis": "【答案】 A （细节题） It would help to protect the environment. 【定位】 P10 But the taxes I suggest aren't that high, less than 3% only. Plus, the money generated would be allocated to environmental protection, which benefits everyone. 但我建议的税率没那么高，只有不到3%。而且，所产生的钱会被用于环境保护，这对每个人都有益。 【信号】 Plus 之后补出关键好处 。她先用 But 澄清税不高，再用 Plus, the money generated would be allocated to environmental protection 补出加税的去向与好处，Plus 引出的这句才是她想强调的作用，是答案句。 【替换】 the money generated would be allocated to environmental protection ↔ It would help to protect the environment. 措施钱去向=保护环境 【排除】 B) 原词陷阱 It would generate money for public health. 借了原文 the money generated，但钱的去向是 environmental protection(环保)而非 public health(公共卫生)，把用途偷换了。 借用原文：the money generated would be allocated to environmental protection C) 未提及 It would need support from the general public. 听着合理，但她谈加税时只说税率低、钱用于环保，从没说这措施「需要公众支持」，是无中生有。 D) 张冠李戴 It would force poor people to change their diet. 含 force 和 poor people，但这是主持人质疑时的说法(第9段)，正是她要反驳的，不是她自己对加税的说法，题干问的是她怎么说。 借用原文：Those taxes could force poor people to adopt your life choices."
